  partName: Right Center Stud
  description: The Right Center Stud is a tiny, complex-shaped component positioned
    at the bottom-right-center of the engine, fabricated from Material.001, which
    serves as a mounting point for various engine components, providing a secure
    and stable connection, and its compact design allows for efficient use of space
    within the engine compartment. The stud's central location subjects it to a unique
    combination of stresses and loads, necessitating careful design and material
    selection. One notable aspect of the Right Center Stud is its role in facilitating
    the installation and removal of engine components, making maintenance and repair
    operations more efficient.
